'' THE LINK RECORD NAMES A LIBRARY ONCE (link-format 2), by the link line's own rule: on
'' windows-x86_64 the name is case-folded and '.dll' dropped, so 'kernel32', 'KERNEL32.dll' (twice,
'' from two declares) and 'Kernel32.DLL' are one entry, under the first spelling. AfxNova's
'' DWM header alone asked for dwmapi.dll 31 times, and the record listed all 31. The record is
'' in the module cache, named by a hash of the exe's path -- not beside the exe.
'' TEST: cli
'' ENV: TKO_MODCACHE=build/.lrd/cache
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' CLEAN: build/.lrd
'' ARGS: build -target windows-x86_64 tests/driver/src/link-record-libs.tiko -o build/.lrd/app.exe
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.lrd/cache/links/*.link :: link-format 2\n
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.lrd/cache/links/*.link :: \nlib kernel32\n
'' EXPECT-FILE-NOT-HAS: build/.lrd/cache/links/*.link :: KERNEL32.dll
'' EXPECT-FILE-NOT-HAS: build/.lrd/cache/links/*.link :: Kernel32.DLL
'' EXPECT-NO-FILE: build/.lrd/app.exe.link
'' RUN: build/.lrd/app.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: ticks
